{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"catlike-oversolemn-flee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote` fails deterministically in this local macOS environment: `git -C <tmp>/bare.git cat-file -t <sha>` exits 128 inside the test's temp bare repo. Verified to fail IDENTICALLY on the untouched main checkout at 6fb4d801c9 with no local changes, so it is environmental/pre-existing, not introduced by any current work. At least six prior closed tickets note the same failure as 'known-unrelated' (e.g. 4522-e600-9e2c-4823, 7851-e06b-9e85-4c9e, 789c-1251-fc21-4cf6) but none left an open tracker, so every session re-diagnoses it.\n\n## Approach\n\nRoot-cause per /rebar-debug: reproduce deterministically, inspect why the object is absent from the bare remote after the push under this git version/filesystem (candidate mechanisms: partial-clone/promisor behaviour, fsmonitor, or APFS temp-dir quirk), and fix the CLASS (test or production ref-lock push), not the one run. No retry/skip band-aid.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause identified with a cited mechanism (recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] The test passes on this environment, or the incompatibility is fixed at its source — verified by running the test 5x locally.\n- [ ] Full reconciler suite green afterwards.","id":"02e8-96bd-82c1-45ff","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote fails on pristine main in local macOS env (git cat-file 128)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787336921704316001,"uuid":"144de8e3-f056-485d-bdac-2bb253032e62"}